Author = {Bhattad, Atul and Priyadarsan, Padhyala},
Title = {Development of thermal conductivity model for alumina hybrid
   nanosuspensions using AI technique},
Journal = {JOURNAL OF THERMAL ANALYSIS AND CALORIMETRY},
Year = {2024},
Volume = {149},
Number = {23},
Pages = {14005-14017},
Month = {DEC},
Abstract = {Substantial studies were made and proposed empirical relationships for
   the thermal conductivity of nanofluids. The influence of nanoparticle
   fraction, shape, size, and thermal behavior of nanoparticles,
   concurrently, is lacking in many of the established thermal conductivity
   relations. This paper proposes a model that reflects the effect of such
   omitted aspects on hybrid nanofluids' thermal conductivity. Various
   Al2O3 hybrid nanofluids having different particle volume concentrations
   (0.1 and 0.01 v\%), shapes (sphere, cylindrical, and flake), and sizes
   were prepared with DI water as base fluid. In a few cases particle ratio
   is changed (0:5, 1:4, 2:3, 3:2, 4:1, 5:0) keeping fixed total particle
   concentration. Various nanoparticle combinations considered are
   AlN-Al2O3, SiC-Al2O3, TiO2-Al2O3, MWCNT-Al2O3, Graphene-Al2O3, and
   MgO-Al2O3. Also, examined the impact of different particle volumetric
   ratios and the liquid temperature (283 K-308 K). Results have shown a
   3.4\% rise in the thermal conductivity of alumina-graphene hybrid
   nanofluids (having 0.01\% volume concentration). A model for the thermal
   conductivity of hybrid nanofluids is developed using the AI technique
   (Symbolic regression) and validated by taking discrete particle size,
   particle volume ratio, thermal conductivity of nanoparticles and base
   fluid, temperature, and shape function into consideration. The
   experimental data were compared with the existing correlation and found
   a deviation of up to 6\%. A comparison of test results with the present
   model indicates a 3.1\% deviation that is acceptable. Hence, the present
   model will provide the thermal conductivity data with accuracy of 3.1\%.
   The proposed formula will reduce the experimental cost and time taken to
   determine the thermal conductivity of alumina-water hybrid suspensions.
   Please check the edit made in the article title.Article title is correct
   Please check the clarity of the sentence `Also, examined the impact of
   different particle \& mldr;'. Correct sentence.},
