   methods, Context-Free Grammars GP (CFG-GP), Grammatical Evolution (GE)
   and Structured Grammatical Evolution (SGE), in the context of the
   complex, real-world problem of predicting the glucose level of people
   with diabetes two hours ahead of time. We concluded that representation
   choice is more impactful with a higher maximum depth, and that CFG-GP
   better explores the search space for deeper trees, achieving better
   results. Furthermore, we find that CFG-GP relies more on feature
   construction, whereas GE and SGE rely more on feature selection.
   Additionally, we altered the GGGP methods in two ways: using \&
